# tools/d/drey_recorder_witness.rish — the recorder controls: samples land only while recording (DREY2).
#
# Season A (Hardware & Right-to-Repair) · waymark DREY · Mikrophone firmware journey · rung DREY2.
# Design read: active-designing/date/20260814/20260814-021722_drey2-recorder-control-state-machine-exploration.md
# Stands on: mikrophone/session.rye (DREY0) — the memory that forgets.
#
# mikrophone/recorder.rye wraps the session that forgets in a control state machine (idle · recording · paused ·
# stopped) whose single invariant is that `feed` reaches `session.capture` ONLY while recording. The selftest proves: a
# sample lands only during a live recording (a feed in idle, paused, or stopped refuses NotRecording before a byte
# moves), the transitions are a real state machine (AlreadyRecording, NotPaused, Stopped each refuse by name), pause
# holds the buffer without forgetting it, and only a recorded-and-committed run carries.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/d/drey_recorder_witness.rish

say "drey-recorder: Language EN — DREY2 gives the Mikrophone its record button: a control state machine over DREY0's session, gating when a sample may land."
say "drey-recorder: Style Radiant — a field recorder is not a raw buffer; nothing is captured unless it is recording, and that promise lives in the control itself."
say "drey-recorder: Lens TAME — four states, a small set of transitions, no heap beyond the session's fixed buffers; feed reaches capture only while recording; every illegal move refuses by name (NotRecording, AlreadyRecording, NotPaused, Stopped); no disk, no network, no key, no funds (custody gate %2 untouched)."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "mikrophone/bin/recorder"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p mikrophone/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build mikrophone/recorder.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "drey-recorder: build failed — ${build.err}"

let outfile = "mikrophone/bin/recorder.out"
let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest > ${outfile} 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "drey-recorder: selftest exited non-zero — see ${outfile}"

let shown = run ["sh" "-c" "cat ${outfile}"]
say "drey-recorder: ${shown.out}"

let green = run ["sh" "-c" "grep -q 'GREEN drey-recorder' ${outfile} && echo yes"]
assert (trim green.out) == "yes" else "drey-recorder: selftest did not print the GREEN drey-recorder line"

say "drey-recorder: GREEN — the Mikrophone recorder gates the session that forgets; a sample lands only while recording. DREY2 lands on a session and a wire both known correct."
